1. Display Characteristics

  - Fully integrated into mobile devices
  - Repairs can be expensive – sometimes better to replace entire unit
  - Hinges and screen durability affect longevity (especially for laptops)
  - Power efficiency directly impacts battery life

2. Display Quality Factors

  - Factor	Description
  - Resolution	Higher = more detail (e.g., 720p, 1080p, 4K)
  - Refresh Rate	Standard: 60 Hz; Higher (120–240 Hz) for gaming/smooth motion
  - Brightness	Important for outdoor use; higher brightness drains battery
  - Contrast	Affects image quality

3. Touchscreen Integration

  - Mobile phones & tablets: Always integrated
  - Laptops: Often optional (check before buying)
  - Touch integration affects usability and power consumption

4. Common Display Issues & Causes

  - Issue	Possible Cause
  - Dim screen	Brightness settings, backlight issue
  - Unresponsive touchscreen	Drivers, digitizer needs recalibration
  - Dead pixels	Hardware defect (usually requires screen replacement)
  - Lines on screen	GPU problem or loose cable connection
  - Flickering	Loose cable or inverter issue
  - Color distortion	Faulty display connection
  - Note: Some issues are settings-related, not hardware failures.

5. Laptop Antennas & Wireless Connectivity

  - Types of Antennas:

    - Wi-Fi antenna (built-in)
    - Bluetooth antenna (built-in)
    - Cellular/LTE/5G antenna (optional, usually in tablets/phones)

  - Common Antenna Issues:

    - Issue	Likely Cause
    - Weak Wi-Fi signal	Too far from source, physical damage
    - Intermittent Bluetooth	Limited range (~30 feet / 10 meters)
    - No cellular service	SIM card issue, roaming settings, network compatibility

  - Antenna Placement:

    - Embedded in screen (typically around edges)
    - Physical damage (dropping) can affect performance

6. Display & Antenna Best Practices

  - Avoid excessive pressure on screen (prevents cracks & dead pixels)
  - Clean with microfiber cloth and screen-safe cleaner
  - Adjust brightness to save battery life
  - Keep device firmware updated
  - Avoid obstructions blocking Wi-Fi/cellular signals
  - Check internal antenna connections if accessible
